{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "vidtoolz.resolveTrustedCaptureShim.v1",
  "title": "Trusted capture shim authority v1.10 (the one shim identity a promotable capture may carry)",
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": [
    "schema",
    "authority_version",
    "shim_version",
    "shim_sha256",
    "shim_source_path",
    "shim_source_sha256",
    "allowlist_digest",
    "allowlist_method_count",
    "codec_version",
    "raw_schema_version",
    "raw_ingest_version",
    "evidence_store_version",
    "trusted_shim_sha256"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "schema": {
      "const": "vidtoolz.resolveTrustedCaptureShim.v1"
    },
    "authority_version": {
      "const": "1.19.0"
    },
    "shim_version": {
      "const": "vidtoolz.captureShim.reference.v1"
    },
    "shim_sha256": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^[a-f0-9]{64}$"
    },
    "shim_source_path": {
      "const": "tools/capture_shim_reference.py"
    },
    "shim_source_sha256": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^[a-f0-9]{64}$"
    },
    "allowlist_digest": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^[a-f0-9]{64}$"
    },
    "allowlist_method_count": {
      "type": "integer",
      "minimum": 1
    },
    "codec_version": {
      "const": "vidtoolz.resolvePyValue.v1"
    },
    "raw_schema_version": {
      "const": "vidtoolz.resolveRawCapabilityCapture.v1"
    },
    "raw_ingest_version": {
      "const": "vidtoolz.resolveRawIngest.v1"
    },
    "evidence_store_version": {
      "const": "vidtoolz.resolveEvidenceStore.v5"
    },
    "trusted_shim_sha256": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^[a-f0-9]{64}$"
    }
  },
  "$comment": "v1.7 (C16-B3): in v1.6 a capture carried capture_shim_version and capture_shim_sha256 that nothing was ever compared against, so a capture claiming any shim sha qualified. Here the bundle pins ONE trusted shim: its source path and source bytes, its own self-hash, the allowlist it may invoke, the codec and raw schema it may emit. trusted_capture_shim() re-verifies all of that against the files on disk on every resolution, and capture_shim_trust_errors() refuses any capture that does not match. This file is itself pinned by FREEZE-MANIFEST.json."
}
